133	70,381,1296,1438	133. Ternately decompound, or four times compound leaf.	A root-leaf of Meadow-Rue: a long footstalk, sheathing at its base, forks into threes again and again and ends in many small, round-lobed leaflets.
134	716,1682,1305,2067	134. Needle-shaped leaves of Larch.	A short piece of Larch branch with two tufts of long, slender, needle-shaped leaves springing from knobby spurs.
135	1357,1278,1687,2067	135. Awl-shaped leaves, &c.	A branch of Red Cedar or Arbor Vitæ, its larger shoots set with sharp awl-shaped leaves and a side branchlet, a, clothed in short, blunt, scale-shaped ones.
